title: 'Registrar: relayed para requests'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      A para with no channel to the registrar parachain can now manage itself through the relay
      chain. It calls the new `pallet-registrar-relay::relay` with a `ParaRequest` (add or remove
      lock, deregister, schedule code upgrade, set current head), which is sent on at once as
      `MessageToParaV1::Relayed`. `pallet-registrar-para` runs it as the new `Origin::RelayedPara`
      and reports the request and its outcome in `RelayedRequest`.

      `pallet-registrar-relay::Config` gains `RelayOrigin`, the paras that may call `relay`
      (`EnsureParachain` for any, `NeverEnsureOrigin` to keep it closed until the migration), and
      `MaxRequestsPerWindow` and `RequestWindow`, which cap the requests one para relays per window.
      A request the transport refuses fails the call and is not counted.

      `pallet-registrar-para::Config` now requires a `RuntimeOrigin` built from its own `Origin`.
      `pallet-registrar-relay`'s `WeightInfo` gains `relay(h)`, `pallet-registrar-para`'s gains
      `receive_relayed(h)`. `MessageToPara` no longer implements `MaxEncodedLen`.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
